<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27766" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διωλύγιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>immense, enormous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήκη δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					890e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μακρὰ . . καὶ δ. φλυαρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					162a
				</span></i>
			 (Sch. expl. both by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιβόητος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοτεινός</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; πράγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					123
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μακρὸς ὁ λόγος καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					2.101d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					111
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤπειρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1258
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Isid.</u>
					303
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					11.146b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμα δ.,</span> of a water-clock
			striking, perh. <i>far-sounding,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				7.641
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>); <i>loud, piercing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθέγμα θρηνῶδες καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Agath.
					1.12
				</span></i>
			: neut. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀνῴμωζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					7.6.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀνεβόησεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Charito
					3.3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Decl.</u>
				26.47
			</span></i>. (Etym. unknown: expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχοῦν
				ἐπὶ πολύ, μέγα καὶ σφοδρόν, διατεταμένον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγα καὶ ἐπὶ πολὺ διῆκον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>)</div>
